;- says nobody knows whom to trust.]  [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON&nbsp- says challenges remain ahead.]  How Americans are stashing billions in savings and checking accounts noted. ", "segment_duration": 260, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63010.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907616, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "PelZbhJyjm", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-08", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907615, "segment_id": "2orexDaJO4", "segment_broadcast_id": "PelZbhJyjm", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Obama Interview (Part I)", "segment_description": "(Indianapolis: Charles Gibson)  How the economy is the topic of conversation along the route of the ABC News bus tour of the Midwest reported; scenes shown from the road into Indiana.  \n\n(Indianapolis: Charles Gibson)  The ABC exclusive interview with Senator Barack Obama presented.  [On the bus, OBAMA&nbsp- says one of the reasons we are doing well is that people look at my consistent approach to the economic crisis; outlines how the administration is hampered by the lack of confidence in President Bush, who has not given a clear sense of what is taking place; states he is saying \"trust in us\" with the job of president to organize the best people to rally the country; indicates now we have \"irrational despair\"; comments on the idealism and passion of the young people.]  \n\n(Indianapolis: Charles Gibson)  Tomorrow's talk with Senator John McCain previewed. ", "segment_duration": 350, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63270.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907617, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type